# Sandbox & Execution Architecture

## Sandbox Provider Interface

Execution is abstracted behind `SandboxProvider` / `SandboxManager` so the underlying provider can be swapped. Providers live in **vendor plugin packages** (see `docs/decisions/0008`): `CloudflareSandboxProvider` in `@catamorphic/cloudflare` (the default — see `docs/decisions/0004` and `CLOUDFLARE.md`) and `DaytonaSandboxProvider` in `@catamorphic/daytona`. `@catamorphic/sandbox` holds only the vendor-neutral contracts and must not depend on vendor SDKs. Hosts construct their chosen provider explicitly at boot and pass it to `createCatamorphic({ sandboxProvider })` — there is no env-sniffing selection helper. Never call the Cloudflare or Daytona SDKs directly from routes — go through the service layer.

Providers handed to `CatamorphicCore` are automatically wrapped with `instrumentSandboxProvider` (OpenTelemetry spans for create/exec/upload/etc.) — do not double-wrap, and keep the wrapper's passthrough of the optional `hydrateWorkspace` method intact when extending the provider contract.

## Execution Model

1. Every invocation creates one canonical `workflow_runs` row. Every Run retains immutable deployed-commit or session-artifact provenance; there is no mutable-source test mode.
2. Production triggering enqueues work in Postgres and returns the Run. Hosts explicitly start `catamorphic.startExecutionWorker(...)`; SDK or plugin construction never starts a worker.
3. Plain Workflows execute as one operation. `defineWorkflow` Runs advance ordered boundary and batch scopes through the same coordinator and Run row.
4. A boundary is one atomic retry scope. A batch owns paged source, per-item replay/retry, optional physical `defineBatchStep` coalescing inside process, and optional sink finalization.
5. Runtime invocations use deployment-scoped supervisors with environment values supplied through provider execution options, never shell assignments. Sequenced events update Postgres transactionally.
6. Public APIs expose capabilities, not execution categories. `stage` and internal runtime work kinds remain private dispatch details.

## Source and execution placement

- **Deployment runtime**: immutable verified capability snapshot beneath
  `.catamorphic/`, tied to its committed artifact. A warm supervisor dispatches
  isolated Bun Workers. Never clone the entire imported repository for execution.
- **Coding-agent workspace**: the selected checkout or managed Allocation holds
  the complete project the agent is working on. Preserve its root files and
  instructions; capability scaffolding stays in `.catamorphic/`.
- **Persistent project data**: a local host may supply `projectDataDirectory` to
  its provider. Deployment runtimes receive `CATAMORPHIC_APP_DATA_DIR` independently
  of immutable source. Build sandboxes do not receive this mount. Cloud execution
  does not imply data synchronization. See ADR 0142 and `INTEGRATION.md`.
- Keep generated plugin references and other temporary staging in host-managed
  storage. The three agent harnesses accept the host's `pluginDirectory`.

## Step Instrumentation Constraints

**Do NOT** use:
- Regex-based source-level code transformation to inject instrumentation.
- Global variable / module-level monkey-patching of ES module exports (ES modules are immutable after evaluation — monkey-patching silently fails).

`@catamorphic/parser` produces an execution transform that wraps exact step call expressions with the node IDs from the parsed graph. Transform only the disposable execution copy, never user source or step declarations.

## Provider Availability

The server degrades gracefully when **no** provider is configured: Run endpoints return `503 Service Unavailable`. Provider
selection is host boot code, not env sniffing inside libraries. The client
surfaces this as a user-visible error, not a crash. Integration tests that
require a specific provider use the `describeIf` skip pattern.

## Coding Agent

The agent is pluggable behind `CodingAgentProvider` (`docs/decisions/0009`, `0018`). Implementations are vendor plugin packages: `@catamorphic/ai-sdk` (**flagship** — Vercel AI SDK's `ToolLoopAgent` runs in the host server process and drives the dev sandbox through `SandboxProvider`; model keys never enter the sandbox) and `@catamorphic/codex` (Codex SDK). Hosts pass one via `createCatamorphic({ codingAgent })`, which enables `core.agentSessions` and the agent HTTP routes. Sessions persist to `agent_sessions` / `agent_messages` with the git commit SHA at session start; per-project agent skills live in the repo under `.catamorphic/skills/` (ADR 0142). Imported projects receive missing framework guidance through the host skill tier without writes to their checkout.
